","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","mistake","miss","forced","good","best","good","best","best","best","best","mistake","miss"],"moments":[{"ply":36,"name":"18…Nce4","cls":"brilliant","color":"b","headline":"18…Nce4!! A real sacrifice: Black gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Leaves the rook on f8 where it can be taken.","White can take, but after 19.Bxf8 Kxf8 20.N5h4 Ng4 the engine rates it +0.14.","The knight joins the attack: it now hits 2 squares around the White king.","Moves the attacked knight to safety.","18…Nce4 gets the knight out of the way of dxc5.","White was threatening dxc5, winning a knight. The knight steps away."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"18…Nce4!! gives up the rook on f8 to stay in the game: after it Black holds the balance (+0.14); anything else leaves Black clearly worse (+2.68)."},{"title":"What Black gives up","text":"18…Nce4 leaves the rook on f8 hanging to the bishop on a3. That's a whole rook on offer."},{"title":"What it does instead","text":"It threatens …Qxf5, winning a knight for a rook."},{"title":"If White takes the rook","text":"19.Bxf8 is met by 19…Kxf8, taking the bishop on f8 and threatening …Qxf5, winning a knight. Then 20…Ng4 threatens …Ngxf2, winning a pawn, and 21…g5 threatens …gxh4, winning a knight. Black ends up a pawn ahead: Black holds the balance (+0.17). This is White's best try."},{"title":"Without the sacrifice","text":"The best move without the sacrifice, 18…Nfe4, is clearly weaker (+2.68 against +0.14). White answers 19.g4, pushing the pawn storm towards the king. That would leave Black clearly worse."}]},{"ply":41,"name":"21.Qxf5","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"21.Qxf5! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the queen on f5.","The next best move, 21.Ne1, would drop White's winning chances from 68% to 39% (−1.19).","21.Qxf5 trades off the attacked queen instead of losing it to …Qxc2 and trades queens.","Black was threatening …Qxc2, winning the queen. The queen takes something with it instead.","Trades queens: the queens come off while ahead, which makes the extra material easier to convert.","The queen on f5 can be taken by the knight on g3."]},{"ply":82,"name":"41…Ra1","cls":"mistake","color":"b","headline":"41…Ra1 is a mistake: Black's winning chances go from 42% to 26%.","points":["White answers 42.Rb6+: the rook joins the attack: it now hits 2 squares around the Black king.","After Rb6+, White wins 1 point of material within 4 moves.","Better was 41…Kd6 (+0.84), which attacks the rook on c7, which is undefended."],"better":"41…Kd6 threatens …Kxc7, winning a rook, and stops Rb6+. Engine line: 42.Rc8 Kd7 43.Rf8 Ke7 44.Rh8 Ra6 (+0.84)."},{"ply":83,"name":"42.Rb6+","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"42.Rb6+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The rook joins the attack: it now hits 2 squares around the Black king.","Gives check, so the reply is forced.","The next best move, 42.Kg2, would drop White's winning chances from 74% to 59% (+1.00).","42.Rb6+ wins a pawn, picking it up with 43.Rxf6.","Sets up a sequence and wins a pawn once the captures settle, picking it up with 43.Rxf6.","Black answers 42…Kd5."]},{"ply":87,"name":"44.e4+","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"44.e4+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Check, and Black has only one legal reply.","The next best move, 44.hxg5, would drop White's winning chances from 84% to 69% (+2.17).","44.e4+ wins a pawn, picking it up with 45.hxg5.","Sets up a sequence and wins a pawn once the captures settle, picking it up with 45.hxg5.","Black answers 44…Kg6, leaving White with a king with pawns missing from its shelter.","Engine line: 44…Kg6 45.hxg5 Rg1+ 46.Kf2 Rxg5 47.Rb8 (+4.30)."]},{"ply":89,"name":"45.hxg5","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"45.hxg5! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the pawn on g5.","Leaves Black with an isolated pawn on h5: a long-term weakness.","The next best move, 45.Rbb7, would drop White's winning chances from 86% to 50% (+0.04).","45.hxg5 stops …gxh4+.","Black was threatening …gxh4+, winning a pawn. hxg5 takes care of it.","Takes the g5 pawn."]},{"ply":99,"name":"50.Rh7+","cls":"miss","color":"w","headline":"50.Rh7+ misses 50.f4, which wins material. White's winning chances go from 99% to 89%.","points":["Black answers 50…Kg5, which attacks the rook on f6, which is undefended.","Better was 50.f4 (+11.82), which pushes the passed pawn to f4."],"better":"50.f4 wins a rook for a pawn, picking it up with 52.fxe5, and threatens Rg5#, with mate in 1. After 50…Ra5 51.e5 Rxe5+ 52.fxe5 Nb4 53.Ke4, White comes out a piece and a pawn up (+11.82)."},{"ply":109,"name":"55.f4","cls":"miss","color":"w","headline":"55.f4 misses the chance 54…Ne1 gave: 55.Rfg7+ would have punished it. White's winning chances go from 96% to 83%.","points":["Black answers 55…Nf3+, which gives check, so the reply is forced.","Better was 55.Rfg7+ (+8.92): the rook takes the open g-file."],"better":"55.Rfg7+ takes the open g-file. Engine line: 55…Kf6 56.e5+ Kf5 57.Rf7+ Kg5 58.Ke4 (+8.92)."}],"opening":{"name":"Zukertort Opening","eco":"A06","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 7…Nbd7: 14 moves in all, 7 by White and 7 by Black.","Theory runs out after 7…Nbd7: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}